aze (2.0.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Remote push transfers missing commits and unshared objects only after
    an announce round-trip; rewritten or unknown tips are refused and
    converged branches are no-ops.
  * Remote pull carries the local tip and applies missing commits and
    unshared objects only, with full-history fallback and three-way merge
    on divergent tips.
  * Tag support through branch specialization: create-tag, delete-tag,
    list-tags, push-tag and pull-tag reuse the branch protocol with object
    type attributes; tag moves are refused and tag names are rejected by
    branch commands.
  * New branch commands list-branches (current branch marked) and
    rename-branch (current pointer moved), backed by engine list operations
    in CRepository.
  * Tag tip resolution moved into CRemoteRepository; client bypass of the
    command layer is forbidden.
  * Default branch renamed from master to main; branch listings no longer
    truncate dotted names.
  * Cache shard base renamed to cache with a centralized file base name.
  * Documentation merged from FEATURES.md into Aze.md with a feature to
    test coverage table and cache structure description; server security
    report added.
  * Server hardening: CAzeServerProcessor decoupled from CAzeServer,
    explicit --bind-address and mandatory --base-path with canonical
    resolution and traversal protection, POST body and push payload limits;
    serve.sh binds 127.0.0.1 and serves the current folder explicitly.
  * Mutual TLS for portal deployments: aze serve --ssl-verify-peer with
    --ssl-ca over a TLS 1.2 floor, peers without a certificate dropped;
    serve.sh gains --verify-peer and --ca on the hardened qt-plus
    CHTTPServer.
  * Packaging and release tooling: scripts/linux/package.sh and
    scripts/linux/release-version.sh added; dead Qt5 deploy plumbing
    removed.
  * Tooling: perf-history.sh supports multi-file random history; the
    massive test exercises intermittent pushes with remote verification.

 -- Jango73 <guillaumed00@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:51:56 +0200

aze (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial Debian packaging, single binary client and server.

